@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `msig-cgl-nouns`
IMPORT `msig-cgl-record`

-- The front of the policy, in the order printed (src:1-49): the recital, the agreement,
-- COVERAGE, SUPPLEMENTARY PAYMENTS, APPLICABLE LAW and JURISDICTION. DEFINITIONS follow
-- in msig-cgl-definitions.l4, CONDITIONS in msig-cgl-conditions.l4.

§ `GENERAL LIABILITY INSURANCE POLICY`
-- src:1 | GENERAL LIABILITY INSURANCE POLICY

§§ `The recital and the agreement`

-- Recitals and the consideration clause decide nothing a rule computes. They are carried
-- as named inert text. What they DO say, that the proposal and declaration are the basis
-- of the Policy, is the representation Condition 10 repeats (msig-cgl-conditions.l4); its
-- consequences for a misstatement are left to the Law on Insurance Business (NOTES.md,
-- fork F31).
-- src:2 | WHEREAS the insured by a proposal and declaration which shall be the basis of this Policy and be deemed to be
-- src:3 | incorporated herein has applied to MSIG Insurance (Vietnam) Company Limited. (the Company) for the insurance
-- src:4 | hereinafter contained
@ref src:2-4
`the recital` MEANS
    "WHEREAS the insured by a proposal and declaration which shall be the basis of this Policy and be deemed to be incorporated herein has applied to MSIG Insurance (Vietnam) Company Limited. (the Company) for the insurance hereinafter contained"

-- The agreement clause has no subject: "In consideration of ... agrees with the named
-- insured as follows". The Company is the party that agrees, from the recital's "(the
-- Company)"; nothing turns on the missing word.
-- src:6 | In consideration of the payment of the premium, in reliance upon the statements in the declaration made a part hereof and
-- src:7 | subject to all of the terms of this Policy, agrees with the named insured as follows:
@ref src:6-7
`the agreement` MEANS
    "In consideration of the payment of the premium, in reliance upon the statements in the declaration made a part hereof and subject to all of the terms of this Policy, agrees with the named insured as follows:"

§§ `COVERAGE`

-- src:10 | COVERAGE
-- src:12 | Coverage is afforded under this Policy in accordance with the specific Coverage Parts identified in the declarations as being
-- src:13 | a part of this Policy.
@ref src:12-13
GIVEN part   IS A `A coverage part`
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the declarations identify` part `as part of` policy MEANS
    elem part (policy's `coverage parts identified in the declarations`)

§§ `SUPPLEMENTARY PAYMENTS`

-- What the Company pays besides damages, "inclusive in the applicable limit of liability":
-- every sum below is counted against the same limit as the damages (src:18). The limit is
-- applied in msig-cgl-answer.l4.
--
-- The two caps are printed in US DOLLARS here (src:28, 34) and in SINGAPORE DOLLARS in
-- the Ultimate Net Loss Clause, which restates (a)-(d) word for word otherwise (src:942,
-- 949). The answer module takes the Ultimate Net Loss Clause as operative (NOTES.md, fork
-- F4); this module encodes the clause as printed here, so that the two can be compared.
-- src:16 | SUPPLEMENTARY PAYMENTS
-- src:18 | The Company will pay, inclusive in the applicable limit of liability:

-- src:20 | (a) all expenses incurred by the Company, all costs taxed against the insured in any suit defended by the Company and all
-- src:21 | interest on the entire amount of any judgement therein which accrues after entry of the judgement and before the
-- src:22 | Company has paid or tendered or deposited in court that part of the judgement which does not exceed the limit of the
-- src:23 | Company's liability thereon;
@ref src:20-23
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Supplementary Payments (a)` sums MEANS
        sums's `expenses incurred by the Company`
    +   sums's `costs taxed against the insured in a suit defended by the Company`
    +   sums's `interest accruing after entry of judgement and before the Company pays, tenders or deposits its part`

-- "not to exceed US$250 per bail bond": each bond capped on its own.
-- "the Company shall have no obligation to apply for or furnish any such bonds": a
-- negative duty, nothing to compute.
-- src:25 | (b) premiums on appeal bonds required in any such suit, premiums on bonds to release attachments in any such suit for
-- src:26 | an amount not in excess of the applicable limit of liability of this Policy, and the cost of bail bonds required of the
-- src:27 | insured because of accident or traffic law violation arising out of the use of any vehicle to which this Policy applies, not
-- src:28 | to exceed US$250 per bail bond, but the Company shall have no obligation to apply for or furnish any such bonds;
@ref src:25-28
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Supplementary Payments (b)` sums rates MEANS
        sums's `premiums on appeal bonds`
    +   sums's `premiums on bonds to release attachments, for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit`
    +   sum (map (GIVEN cost YIELD min cost (250 TIMES rates's `dong per United States dollar`)) (sums's `the cost of each bail bond`))

-- src:30 | (c) expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of an accident, for bodily injury to which this Policy
-- src:31 | applies;
@ref src:30-31
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Supplementary Payments (c)` sums MEANS
    sums's `expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of the accident`

-- "including actual loss of earnings not to exceed US$25 per day": each day capped.
-- src:33 | (d) reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request in assisting the Company in the investigation
-- src:34 | or defence of any claim or suit, including actual loss of earnings not to exceed US$25 per day.
@ref src:33-34
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Supplementary Payments (d)` sums rates MEANS
        sums's `reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request, other than loss of earnings`
    +   sum (map (GIVEN earnings YIELD min earnings (25 TIMES rates's `dong per United States dollar`)) (sums's `the actual loss of earnings for each day`))

@ref src:16-34
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Supplementary Payments, as printed with US dollar caps` sums rates MEANS
        `Supplementary Payments (a)` sums
    +   `Supplementary Payments (b)` sums rates
    +   `Supplementary Payments (c)` sums
    +   `Supplementary Payments (d)` sums rates

§§ `APPLICABLE LAW`

-- A choice of law and of forum. It selects the law under which every other clause is
-- read; it adds no condition of payment, so it is carried as named text. The Law on
-- Insurance Business 08/2022/QH15 is that law's statute on insurance contracts; where it
-- bears on a clause, NOTES.md records it as a LAW fork.
-- src:37 | APPLICABLE LAW
-- src:39 | This contract of insurance is governed by and is to be construed in accordance with the laws of Vietnam. The court of
-- src:40 | competent jurisdiction in Vietnam shall have the exclusive jurisdiction over all matters relating to the construction, validity
-- src:41 | and performance of this contract of insurance.
@ref src:39-41
`the applicable law` MEANS
    "This contract of insurance is governed by and is to be construed in accordance with the laws of Vietnam. The court of competent jurisdiction in Vietnam shall have the exclusive jurisdiction over all matters relating to the construction, validity and performance of this contract of insurance."

§§ `JURISDICTION`

-- This one is operative: it takes a judgement out of the indemnity. It speaks only of
-- JUDGEMENTS, so a liability fixed by settlement is untouched by it (NOTES.md, fork F2).
-- src:44 | JURISDICTION
-- src:46 | The indemnity provided by this Policy shall not apply in respect of judgements which are not in the first instance delivered by
-- src:47 | or obtained from a Court of competent jurisdiction within the Socialist Republic of Vietnam nor to orders obtained in the said
-- src:48 | Court for the enforcement of judgements made outside the Socialist Republic of Vietnam whether by way of reciprocal
-- src:49 | agreements or otherwise.
@ref src:46-49
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Jurisdiction clause takes the judgement outside the indemnity` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured's liability for the damages is fixed by a judgement`
    AND (   NOT `for` claim `,` `the judgement was delivered in the first instance by, or obtained from, a court of competent jurisdiction within Vietnam`
         OR `for` claim `,` `the judgement is an order of a Vietnamese court for the enforcement of a judgement made outside Vietnam`)
